<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/MODEL/" xmlns:dmndi="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/DMNDI/" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20180521/DC/" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20180521/DI/" id="Confirm_isolation" name="4.4.4 Confirm isolation and permit-to-work" namespace="http://tim-method.example/utility-wam/1.0" exporter="Utility WAM Industry Process Reference" exporterVersion="2026-08-28">
  <description>THIS TABLE VERIFIES. IT DOES NOT ISSUE. 18.4.4 is the only process in this model that issues a clearance, and it is the system operator who gives it under 29 CFR 1910.269(m)(3)(vi). What the crew does here is establish which energy-control regime governs, confirm the control actually exists and is valid, and BLOCK the work when it does not.

The regimes do not substitute for one another and the rows say so. 1910.269(m) governs electric transmission and distribution. 1910.147 lockout/tagout reaches gas distribution work precisely because 1910.147(a)(1)(ii)(C) excludes electric utility installations. Complying with the wrong one is not partial compliance - 1910.269(m)(1) treats a conductor deenergized under anything other than (d) or (m) as still energized.

And a permit is not a clearance. A permit comes from an external authority and is obtained at 2.5; a clearance is an internal act of the system operator. A crew holding a street-opening permit and no clearance has authority to dig and none to touch the plant.</description>
  <inputData id="in_regime" name="Energy-control regime from 18.1.1"><variable id="in_regime_v" name="Energy-control regime from 18.1.1" typeRef="string"/></inputData>
  <inputData id="in_controlExists" name="The clearance or lockout is in place"><variable id="in_controlExists_v" name="The clearance or lockout is in place" typeRef="boolean"/></inputData>
  <inputData id="in_verified" name="Verified with the issuing authority"><variable id="in_verified_v" name="Verified with the issuing authority" typeRef="boolean"/></inputData>
  <inputData id="in_withinLimits" name="Work is within the recorded limits of the control"><variable id="in_withinLimits_v" name="Work is within the recorded limits of the control" typeRef="boolean"/></inputData>
  <knowledgeSource id="ks_269m3" name="29 CFR 1910.269(m)(1), (m)(3)(vi) and (m)(3)(viii); 29 CFR 1910.147(a)(1)(ii)(C); 18.4.4"><description>(m)(3)(vi) the system operator gives the clearance; (m)(3)(viii) only then may the lines be considered deenergized; (m)(1) anything else is treated as energized. 1910.147(a)(1)(ii)(C) is the exclusion that puts gas under lockout/tagout.</description></knowledgeSource>
  <decision id="d_4_4_4" name="Authority to work">
    <variable id="d_4_4_4_v" name="Authority to work" typeRef="string"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_d_4_4_4_ks_269m3"><requiredInput href="#ks_269m3"/></informationRequirement>
    <decisionTable id="d_4_4_4_dt" hitPolicy="FIRST" preferredOrientation="Rule-as-Row">
      <input id="d_4_4_4_i1" label="Regime"><inputExpression id="d_4_4_4_i1_e" typeRef="string"><text>in_regime</text></inputExpression></input>
      <input id="d_4_4_4_i2" label="Control in place"><inputExpression id="d_4_4_4_i2_e" typeRef="boolean"><text>in_controlExists</text></inputExpression></input>
      <input id="d_4_4_4_i3" label="Verified with the issuer"><inputExpression id="d_4_4_4_i3_e" typeRef="boolean"><text>in_verified</text></inputExpression></input>
      <input id="d_4_4_4_i4" label="Within recorded limits"><inputExpression id="d_4_4_4_i4_e" typeRef="boolean"><text>in_withinLimits</text></inputExpression></input>
      <output id="d_4_4_4_o" label="Authority to work" name="Authority to work" typeRef="string"/>
      <rule id="d_4_4_4_r1">
        <description>No isolation required. Work proceeds on the live-line or no-contact method, and 1910.269(l) minimum approach distance governs instead. No clearance exists, so there is nothing for 18.5 to release.</description>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r1_ie1"><text>"noIsolation"</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r1_ie2"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r1_ie3"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r1_ie4"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r1_oe"><text>"proceedLiveMethod"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_4_4_4_r2">
        <description>BLOCK. No clearance and no lockout in place. 1910.269(m)(1) treats the plant as energized whatever has been done to it, and the crew requests one through 18.4.4 rather than proceeding.</description>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r2_ie1"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r2_ie2"><text>false</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r2_ie3"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r2_ie4"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r2_oe"><text>"blockNoControl"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_4_4_4_r3">
        <description>BLOCK. A control the crew believes exists but has not confirmed with the issuing authority is a belief. (m)(3)(vi) makes the giving of the clearance an act of the system operator, so the system operator is who confirms it.</description>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r3_ie1"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r3_ie2"><text>true</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r3_ie3"><text>false</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r3_ie4"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r3_oe"><text>"blockUnverified"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_4_4_4_r4">
        <description>BLOCK. Valid control, but the work has moved outside the section, the equipment or the time it covers. 18.4.6 extends or transfers; the crew does not widen the scope of a clearance by working past it.</description>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r4_ie1"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r4_ie2"><text>true</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r4_ie3"><text>true</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r4_ie4"><text>false</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r4_oe"><text>"blockOutsideLimits"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_4_4_4_r5">
        <description>Proceed under 29 CFR 1910.147, which reaches gas because (a)(1)(ii)(C) excludes only electric utility installations. The gas section is proved safe by purge and atmosphere at 18.4.3, never by a test for voltage.</description>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r5_ie1"><text>"gasOperating"</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r5_ie2"><text>true</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r5_ie3"><text>true</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r5_ie4"><text>true</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r5_oe"><text>"proceedLotoGas"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_4_4_4_r6">
        <description>Proceed. The clearance 18.4.4 issued is held, verified and covers this work. (m)(3)(viii) has been satisfied and the section may be treated as deenergized.</description>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r6_ie1"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r6_ie2"><text>true</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r6_ie3"><text>true</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r6_ie4"><text>true</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r6_oe"><text>"proceedUnderClearance"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_4_4_4_r7">
        <description>Regime not established. 18.1.1 returns it and this table consumes it - and the default here is the one (m)(1) punishes.</description>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r7_ie1"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r7_ie2"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r7_ie3"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r7_ie4"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_4_4_4_r7_oe"><text>"determineManually"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
    </decisionTable>
  </decision>
  <dmndi:DMNDI>
    <dmndi:DMNDiagram id="drd_Confirm_isolation">
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="sh_in_regime" dmnElementRef="in_regime"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="420" width="160" height="45"/></dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="sh_in_controlExists" dmnElementRef="in_controlExists"><dc:Bounds x="245" y="420" width="160" height="45"/></dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="sh_in_verified" dmnElementRef="in_verified"><dc:Bounds x="430" y="420" width="160" height="45"/></dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="sh_in_withinLimits" dmnElementRef="in_withinLimits"><dc:Bounds x="615" y="420" width="160" height="45"/></dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="sh_d_4_4_4" dmnElementRef="d_4_4_4"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="240" width="180" height="70"/></dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="sh_ks_269m3" dmnElementRef="ks_269m3"><dc:Bounds x="900" y="100" width="160" height="55"/></dmndi:DMNShape>
    </dmndi:DMNDiagram>
  </dmndi:DMNDI>
</definitions>
